Sorry, I realized that one must quit the spell screen so actually there 
is one keypress more if you adjust only one spell vs. one item: +, a, b, 
esc vs. meta-a, a, b.

But if you adjust more than one at a time your keypresses are equal (for 
2) or less (3 or more): +, a, b, c, d, e, f, esc vs. meta-a, a, b, 
meta-a, c, d, meta-a, e, f.

One can argue that one way to adjust is cheaper if adjusting is done in 
batch and the other is cheaper if one adjusts once a while. This makes 
sense for spells as when you change the new learned spell for another 
letter you might chnage others at the same time.

